IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P8-gate`

-- P8-art79: Article 79, procedure at national level for dealing with AI systems presenting a risk. LAYER 1.
-- Group General (from 2 August 2026). Article 79 has no `▼M1` passage. It provides seam S11: `the market surveillance authority has found under Article 79 that the AI system presents a risk` (PLAN.md section 4),
-- the input of Articles 80 to 83 (another part). The Article asks questions about one AI system, so the gate is the group's, asked with the route, the placement date and the design-change fact.
-- "15 working days" needs a calendar of working days that the text does not give: the asker supplies the number of days that the 15 working days cover.
-- The consolidated text is a rendering with no legal effect.

DECLARE `Art 79 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 79(2) carry out an evaluation of the AI system concerned in respect of its compliance with all the requirements and obligations laid down in this Regulation`
    `Art 79(2) give particular attention to AI systems presenting a risk to vulnerable groups`
    `Art 79(2) inform and fully cooperate with the relevant national public authorities or bodies referred to in Article 77(1)`
    `Art 79(2) cooperate as necessary with the market surveillance authority and with the other national public authorities or bodies referred to in Article 77(1)`
    `Art 79(2) require the relevant operator to take all appropriate corrective actions to bring the AI system into compliance, to withdraw the AI system from the market, or to recall it`
    `Art 79(2) take all appropriate corrective actions within the period`
    `Art 79(2) inform the relevant notified body`
    `Art 79(3) inform the Commission and the other Member States without undue delay of the results of the evaluation and of the actions that the operator is required to take`
    `Art 79(4) ensure that all appropriate corrective action is taken in respect of all the AI systems concerned that the operator has made available on the Union market`
    `Art 79(5) take all appropriate provisional measures to prohibit or restrict the AI system's being made available on its national market or put into service, to withdraw the product or the standalone AI system from that market or to recall it`
    `Art 79(5) notify the Commission and the other Member States of those provisional measures without undue delay`
    `Art 79(6) include all available details in the notification`
    `Art 79(7) inform the Commission and the other Member States of any measures adopted and of any additional information at their disposal relating to the non-compliance`
    `Art 79(7) inform the Commission and the other Member States of their objections to the notified national measure`
    `Art 79(9) ensure that appropriate restrictive measures are taken in respect of the product or the AI system concerned without undue delay`

DECLARE `Art 79(6) cause of the non-compliance` IS ONE OF
    `Art 79(6)(a) non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5`
    `Art 79(6)(b) a failure of a high-risk AI system to meet requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2`
    `Art 79(6)(c) shortcomings in the harmonised standards or common specifications referred to in Articles 40 and 41 conferring a presumption of conformity`
    `Art 79(6)(d) non-compliance with Article 50`
    `Art 79(6) any other cause that the list does not name`

§ `Article 79(1): AI systems presenting a risk, and seam S11`

-- src:1299 | 1. AI systems presenting a risk shall be understood as a ‘product presenting a risk’ as defined in Article 3, point 19 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020, in so far as they present risks to the health or safety, or to fundamental rights, of persons.
@ref Art 79(1) (src:1299)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system presents risks to the health or safety, or to fundamental rights, of persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 79(1) the AI system presenting a risk is understood as a product presenting a risk as defined in Article 3, point 19 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives, and Art 111(2) saves a high-risk AI system placed earlier and not significantly changed
    ELSE IF `the AI system presents risks to the health or safety, or to fundamental rights, of persons`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence applies "in so far as they present risks to the health or safety, or to fundamental rights, of persons": a limit with no "only" (ruling (c))

-- Seam S11 (PLAN.md section 4): Articles 80 to 83 take this question as a BOOLEAN input. Its FALSE means "not shown on these facts", never "shown not to present a risk" (the maybe-type function above carries the difference).
-- src:1299 | 1. AI systems presenting a risk shall be understood as a ‘product presenting a risk’ as defined in Article 3, point 19 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020, in so far as they present risks to the health or safety, or to fundamental rights, of persons.
-- src:1300 | 2. Where the market surveillance authority of a Member State has sufficient reason to consider an AI system to present a risk as referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article, it shall carry out an evaluation of the AI system concerned in respect of its compliance with all the requirements and obligations laid down in this Regulation. Particular attention shall be given to AI systems presenting a risk to vulnerable groups. Where risks to fundamental rights are identified, the market surveillance authority shall also inform and fully cooperate with the relevant national public authorities or bodies referred to in Article 77(1). The relevant operators shall cooperate as necessary with the market surveillance authority and with the other national public authorities or bodies referred to in Article 77(1).
@ref Art 79(1) and Art 79(2) first sentence (src:1299-1300)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system presents risks to the health or safety, or to fundamental rights, of persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the market surveillance authority of a Member State has sufficient reason to consider the AI system to present a risk as referred to in paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 79(2) the market surveillance authority has found under Article 79 that the AI system presents a risk` MEANS
        `Art 79(1) the AI system presenting a risk is understood as a product presenting a risk as defined in Article 3, point 19 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` `the AI system presents risks to the health or safety, or to fundamental rights, of persons` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    AND `the market surveillance authority of a Member State has sufficient reason to consider the AI system to present a risk as referred to in paragraph 1`

§ `Article 79(2): the evaluation`

-- src:1300 | 2. Where the market surveillance authority of a Member State has sufficient reason to consider an AI system to present a risk as referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article, it shall carry out an evaluation of the AI system concerned in respect of its compliance with all the requirements and obligations laid down in this Regulation. Particular attention shall be given to AI systems presenting a risk to vulnerable groups. Where risks to fundamental rights are identified, the market surveillance authority shall also inform and fully cooperate with the relevant national public authorities or bodies referred to in Article 77(1). The relevant operators shall cooperate as necessary with the market surveillance authority and with the other national public authorities or bodies referred to in Article 77(1).
@ref Art 79(2) first subparagraph, first sentence (src:1300)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the market surveillance authority of a Member State has sufficient reason to consider the AI system to present a risk as referred to in paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 79(2) first sentence the market surveillance authority must carry out an evaluation of the AI system concerned` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives, and Art 111(2) saves a high-risk AI system placed earlier and not significantly changed
    ELSE IF `the market surveillance authority of a Member State has sufficient reason to consider the AI system to present a risk as referred to in paragraph 1`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the market surveillance authority of a Member State has sufficient reason to consider an AI system to present a risk as referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article, it shall carry out an evaluation" (an unmet "where" gate counts as the text's no: ruling (b)) (fork F-79-2-first-duty)

-- src:1300 | 2. Where the market surveillance authority of a Member State has sufficient reason to consider an AI system to present a risk as referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article, it shall carry out an evaluation of the AI system concerned in respect of its compliance with all the requirements and obligations laid down in this Regulation. Particular attention shall be given to AI systems presenting a risk to vulnerable groups. Where risks to fundamental rights are identified, the market surveillance authority shall also inform and fully cooperate with the relevant national public authorities or bodies referred to in Article 77(1). The relevant operators shall cooperate as necessary with the market surveillance authority and with the other national public authorities or bodies referred to in Article 77(1).
@ref Art 79(2) first subparagraph, first sentence (src:1300)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the market surveillance authority of a Member State has sufficient reason to consider the AI system to present a risk as referred to in paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 79 act`
`Art 79(2) first sentence the market surveillance authority's duty to carry out an evaluation` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)) OR (NOT `the market surveillance authority of a Member State has sufficient reason to consider the AI system to present a risk as referred to in paragraph 1`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group General does not apply on the date asked, the system is saved by Art 111(2), or the conditions of the duty are not met
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party market surveillance authority`
        MUST `Art 79(2) carry out an evaluation of the AI system concerned in respect of its compliance with all the requirements and obligations laid down in this Regulation`
        HENCE FULFILLED

